From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:34:47 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 28/28] tst_qquickvideostereo: the depth views on the GPU, the
 colour a pass turns the planes into, the way chosen and told

The earlier depth tests draw with a fixed way on the processor; new tests: the defaults are the library's, picking a warping or a gap
filling turns the automatic way off, the choice is told with the frame rate and the budget and is kept in the person's cache, the GPU
draws the same views as the C code, from several threads in turn, and the colour of limited and full range YUV 4:2:0, NV12, NV21 and
YV12 in BT.601, BT.709 and BT.2020 is what the matrices give.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 via Claude Code
Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
